<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The widget on Android 8-11; Android 12 and later read res/xml-v31/diditake_widget_info.xml (targetCell, and the
    rest of the reasons). Default and smallest size: the launcher's real 4x2 cells (REQ-026, decided 2026-11-12
    19:11 KST).

    Launcher3 before Android 12 has no targetCell: it places the widget at the count of minWidth/Height and lets it
    shrink to the count of minResizeWidth/Height, with cells = ceil((size + 16dp) / cell), the smaller cell of the
    upright and the turned home screen, the system's widget padding (8dp a side) and no spacing. Pixel Launcher on the
    Pixel 5 emulator (scripts/emulator/widget_size_check.py, run 43608286853, BUG-005) has 5 columns at 393dp and at
    360dp wide: cells 73.0 and 75.3dp wide at 393dp, 67.0 and 68.6dp at 360dp (API 30, 26), turned rows 64.0-70.5dp.
    - width 230dp: 246dp with the padding, above three cells (at most 225.8dp) and within four (at least 268.0dp). The
      270dp of Android 12 and later did not fit four cells at 360dp: the widget was placed 5x2 there.
    - height 102dp: 118dp with the padding, above one turned row (at most 70.5dp) and within two (at least 128.0dp).
    targetCellWidth/Height are left out: these versions ignore them. updatePeriodMillis 0, configure and
    widgetFeatures: as in res/xml-v31 (the Reconfigure button comes from Android 12).
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:configure="com.judangbang.pillbadeum.widget.WidgetPickActivity"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/glance_default_loading_layout"
    android:minWidth="230dp"
    android:minHeight="102dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="230dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="102dp"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:widgetFeatures="reconfigurable" />
